The portable C in the scenario setup-config-mouse: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of
harness/goldens/setup-config-mouse.txt, see harness/goldens.py: a line with -
is the golden's, a line with + is what is expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 7 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the Configuration of the setup has no Memory allocation and no TSR
manager: Execute options is one line, Quick execute commands, and the Keyboard
options stand two rows further up, with the last two rows of the right half
empty. The clicks on Quick execute commands and on Alt alone selects menu are
a row and two rows further up, and the mouse pointer with them. The mouse
pointer exchanges the colours of the cell that it is on, the middle of the
screen where nothing has moved it: the lines have moved under it, and it stays

